// codebox_halftone.gen -- f_halftone: the one stage. Tone to marks on a fixed-angle lattice, one plate per color channel.
// Stateless, per pixel. Float32. Mirror: tests/modules/halftone/halftone_mirror.halftone_stage() (the conventions in its
// docstring are the ones followed here). T020: Dot and Line, soft edge, exact extremes, zap, bypass, alpha; the per-plate
// phase (FR-016) is in because it is part of the lattice formula. 2026-11-14: shape (T023), jitter (T024), Threshold and
// Bayer (T025), the Single plate mode (T016b).
//
// Lattice (plan ADR-1): p = ((u - .5) * aspect, v - .5) in frame heights; q = R(-angle) p / pitch - phase;
//   lattice cell = floor(q + .5), local f = q - that, in [-.5, .5]^2.
// Spot functions (ADR-2): Dot T = A(r), the area of the radius-r circle inside the unit cell; Line T = 2 |f_y|.
//   dot_shape (T023, Dot only; a Param named `shape` never received its value on the bench, 2026-11-14) morphs round to square: T = mix(A(r), (2 max(|f_x|, |f_y|))^2, shape), the slope likewise.
// Soft edge (ADR-3): coverage = clamp(.5 + (tone - T) / w, 0, 1), w = max(softness / 2, aa) * |dT/dd|,
//   aa = 1 / (pitch in texels); then tone <= 0 gives exactly 0 and tone >= 1 exactly 1.
// Tone (ADR-4): ONE nearest read per plate at a texel centre: Dot at the lattice cell's centre, Line at the pixel's own
//   position along its centreline row. The reads are in the main body, the tone is passed to the functions (gate G8).
// Jitter (ADR-5, Dot only): each cell centre moves by jitter * .5 * (hash - .5) cells (the sin hash, seeded); the nine cells
//   around the pixel are tested and the largest coverage wins; the tone is read at each displaced centre. jitter 0 takes the
//   one-cell path, so the regular lattice is exactly the T020 one. Each jittered mark is clipped to its own displaced unit
//   square (fix A, Matt 2026-11-14), as the mirror does.
// Threshold (ADR-6): smoothstep(level - w, level + w, tone), w = softness / 2 (a hard step at softness 0), per pixel.
// Bayer: the 8 x 8 ordered matrix by texel, M = sum over bits b of 4^(2-b) (2 (x_b xor y_b) + y_b); lit where tone > (M + .5) / 64.
//   The matrix repeats once per pitch (Matt, 2026-11-14): a cell is pitch / 8 frame heights, rounded to whole pixels, at
//   least 1. bayer_cell 1 (default; Matt, 2026-11-14) reads one tone per cell at its centre pixel, a true ordered dither;
//   0 reads it per pixel (a threshold at each cell's level). Identical at 1-pixel cells.
// Per-plate pitch (T029b, Matt 2026-11-14, FR-022): a plate's pitch is pitch * scale_<plate>; every length above that says
//   "pitch" means the plate's own pitch. Single uses scale_b. bay_cell returns four values (inferred to compile; the bench decides).
// Single plate (T016b, plate_mode 1; spec "Plates from f_separate"): the whole texture is ONE plate at angle_b and phase_b.
//   Its tone is the brightest channel, t = max(r, g, b), at the read texel; the colour is rgb / t there (black when t <= 0); the
//   output is that colour times the coverage. The colour texel is the one the tone came from: the cell centre (displaced when
//   jittered) for Dot, the centreline point for Line, the pixel's own for Threshold and Bayer.
// Plates (T028, Matt 2026-11-14; spec US9, FR-017 to FR-021, plan ADR-8): plate_mode 2 screens the module's inlets 1 to 3
//   (gen in2 to in4) each as Single, plate 1 at the R angle / phase / scale, 2 at G, 3 at B; summed and clamped to 0..1; alpha
//   the largest of the connected plates' alphas. An unconnected plate is skipped by its connected flag (plate1_on etc., from
//   vs_inState), never by its value: an unconnected inlet reads black with alpha 1, which would set alpha to 1. Inlet 0 is
//   ignored except by bypass. The Single path is the function single_path; `src` picks the inlet (0 = in1 ... 3 = in4).
// Blue and Random (T035, Matt 2026-11-14; spec US10, FR-023 to FR-026, plan ADR-10): screens 4 and 5, Bayer's grain cell
//   and Read, the threshold from the void-and-cluster pattern (gen in5: package/media/f_bluenoise64.jxf through the builder's
//   static mod inlet, 64 x 64, tiled, nearest) or the sin hash of the cell. The cell index is shifted by the plate's offset
//   ((0, 0), (23, 41), (47, 13) for plates 0 / 1 / 2; Single is plate 2, Plates plate k is k - 1), by the phase in whole
//   grain cells (8 per pitch, rounded), and for Blue by (61, 29) per seed step; Random hashes the shifted cell with the seed.
//   All offsets preliminary (Claude, T033 spike); the mirror's dither_threshold is the reference. Inferred, for the bench: that
//   the one-plane float texture reads its value in .x, and that its row 0 is the smallest norm.y.
// Levels (T035, FR-027, ADR-11): Bayer, Blue and Random: q = tone (L - 1); out = (floor(q) + [fract(q) > threshold]) / (L - 1),
//   clamped, tone <= 0 exactly 0, tone >= 1 exactly 1. At L = 2 it is the one-bit dither, bit for bit.
// screen: 0 = Dot, 1 = Line, 2 = Threshold, 3 = Bayer, 4 = Blue, 5 = Random. Angles in degrees. bypass_gate = 1: the (zapped) source.
// Non-finite input is zapped to 0: abs(x) < 1e30 with switch() (NaN == NaN is TRUE on this GPU).
// The render size comes from the Params `width` and `height` (render_dim; the size global reads 1 inside a live Vsynth pix,
// build/spec.md). A bench job must set both to the output's size.
zap(xv) {
    return switch(abs(xv) < 1e30, xv, 0);
}

// cos and sin of exact quarter turns come out as 1e-8, not 0: snap, so 0 and 90 degrees sit on the pixel grid (G6)
snap0(xv) {
    return switch(abs(xv) < 0.000001, 0, xv);
}

area_round(rad) {
    rc = min(rad, 0.70710678);
    inner = pi * rc * rc;
    ac = acos(clamp(1 / (2 * max(rc, 0.000001)), 0, 1));
    seg = rc * rc * ac - 0.5 * sqrt(max(rc * rc - 0.25, 0));
    area = switch(rc > 0.5, inner - 4 * seg, inner);
    return switch(rad >= 0.70710678, 1, area);
}

area_slope(rad) {
    rc = min(rad, 0.70710678);
    ac = acos(clamp(1 / (2 * max(rc, 0.000001)), 0, 1));
    slp = switch(rc <= 0.5, twopi * rc, rc * (twopi - 8 * ac));
    return switch(rad >= 0.70710678, 0, slp);
}

// lattice coordinates of the position (px, py)
lat_xy(px, py, cs, sn, pit, phx, phy) {
    return (cs * px + sn * py) / pit - phx, (cs * py - sn * px) / pit - phy;
}

// where the plate's tone is read: normalized coordinates of a texel centre, clamped to the frame
read_uv(qx, qy, is_line, cs, sn, pit, phx, phy, asp, wd, ht) {
    xx = switch(is_line > 0.5, qx, floor(qx + 0.5)) + phx;
    yy = floor(qy + 0.5) + phy;
    ppx = (cs * xx - sn * yy) * pit;
    ppy = (sn * xx + cs * yy) * pit;
    ti = clamp(floor((ppx / asp + 0.5) * wd), 0, wd - 1);
    tj = clamp(floor((ppy + 0.5) * ht), 0, ht - 1);
    return (ti + 0.5) / wd, (tj + 0.5) / ht;
}

// coverage at local lattice coordinates (fx, fy) relative to a mark's centre
cover_local(fx, fy, is_line, tone, soft, aa, shp) {
    rad = sqrt(fx * fx + fy * fy);
    sq = max(abs(fx), abs(fy));
    thr_dot = mix(area_round(rad), 4 * sq * sq, shp);
    slp_dot = mix(area_slope(rad), 8 * sq, shp);
    thr = switch(is_line > 0.5, 2 * abs(fy), thr_dot);
    slp = switch(is_line > 0.5, 2, slp_dot);
    wid = max(soft * 0.5, aa) * max(abs(slp), 0.000001);
    cov = clamp(0.5 + (tone - thr) / wid, 0, 1);
    return switch(tone <= 0, 0, switch(tone >= 1, 1, cov));
}

cover(qx, qy, is_line, tone, soft, aa, shp) {
    return cover_local(qx - floor(qx + 0.5), qy - floor(qy + 0.5), is_line, tone, soft, aa, shp);
}

// the zapped tone at a texel centre: ch 0 r, 1 g, 2 b, 3 the brightest of the three (Single); src the inlet (0 = in1 ... 3 = in4)
rd(ru, rv, ch, src) {
    tx = 0;
    ty = 0;
    tz = 0;
    if (src < 0.5) {
        tx = zap(nearest(in1, vec(ru, rv)).x);
        ty = zap(nearest(in1, vec(ru, rv)).y);
        tz = zap(nearest(in1, vec(ru, rv)).z);
    } else if (src < 1.5) {
        tx = zap(nearest(in2, vec(ru, rv)).x);
        ty = zap(nearest(in2, vec(ru, rv)).y);
        tz = zap(nearest(in2, vec(ru, rv)).z);
    } else if (src < 2.5) {
        tx = zap(nearest(in3, vec(ru, rv)).x);
        ty = zap(nearest(in3, vec(ru, rv)).y);
        tz = zap(nearest(in3, vec(ru, rv)).z);
    } else {
        tx = zap(nearest(in4, vec(ru, rv)).x);
        ty = zap(nearest(in4, vec(ru, rv)).y);
        tz = zap(nearest(in4, vec(ru, rv)).z);
    }
    return switch(ch < 0.5, tx, switch(ch < 1.5, ty, switch(ch < 2.5, tz, max(max(tx, ty), tz))));
}

// T016b: the read texel of the pixel's own cell centre, displaced by the jitter (the Single colour under jitter)
jit_uv(qx, qy, cs, sn, pit, phx, phy, asp, wd, ht, jit, sd) {
    nx = floor(qx + 0.5);
    ny = floor(qy + 0.5);
    hx = fract(sin(nx * 127.1 + ny * 311.7 + sd * 74.7) * 43758.5453);
    hy = fract(sin(nx * 269.5 + ny * 183.3 + sd * 246.1) * 43758.5453);
    xx = nx + jit * 0.5 * (hx - 0.5) + phx;
    yy = ny + jit * 0.5 * (hy - 0.5) + phy;
    ppx = (cs * xx - sn * yy) * pit;
    ppy = (sn * xx + cs * yy) * pit;
    ti = clamp(floor((ppx / asp + 0.5) * wd), 0, wd - 1);
    tj = clamp(floor((ppy + 0.5) * ht), 0, ht - 1);
    return (ti + 0.5) / wd, (tj + 0.5) / ht;
}

// T024: the jittered Dot. ch picks the plate's channel (0 r, 1 g, 2 b, 3 the brightest: Single). Reads inside a function and a loop are exact (T010).
dot_jit(qx, qy, ch, src, cs, sn, pit, phx, phy, asp, wd, ht, soft, aa, shp, jit, sd) {
    cx = floor(qx + 0.5);
    cy = floor(qy + 0.5);
    best = 0;
    for (j = 0; j < 3; j += 1) {
        for (i = 0; i < 3; i += 1) {
            nx = cx + i - 1;
            ny = cy + j - 1;
            hx = fract(sin(nx * 127.1 + ny * 311.7 + sd * 74.7) * 43758.5453);
            hy = fract(sin(nx * 269.5 + ny * 183.3 + sd * 246.1) * 43758.5453);
            gx = nx + jit * 0.5 * (hx - 0.5);
            gy = ny + jit * 0.5 * (hy - 0.5);
            xx = gx + phx;
            yy = gy + phy;
            ppx = (cs * xx - sn * yy) * pit;
            ppy = (sn * xx + cs * yy) * pit;
            ti = clamp(floor((ppx / asp + 0.5) * wd), 0, wd - 1);
            tj = clamp(floor((ppy + 0.5) * ht), 0, ht - 1);
            ru = (ti + 0.5) / wd;
            rv = (tj + 0.5) / ht;
            tone = rd(ru, rv, ch, src);
            // fix A (Matt, 2026-11-14): a mark lives only in its own displaced unit square (unclipped, a full-tone
            // neighbour inked the whole 3 x 3 block, since tone >= 1 gives full ink at any distance)
            inside = step(max(abs(qx - gx), abs(qy - gy)), 0.5);
            best = max(best, inside * cover_local(qx - gx, qy - gy, 0, tone, soft, aa, shp));
        }
    }
    return best;
}

// T025: the Threshold and Bayer coverage of one per-pixel tone
thresh(tone, lvl, soft) {
    hw = soft * 0.5;
    return switch(hw > 0, smoothstep(lvl - hw, lvl + hw, tone), switch(tone > lvl, 1, 0));
}

// T035: the dither screens. kind 0 Bayer, 1 Blue, 2 Random; plt the plate (0, 1, 2); lv the levels.
dither(tone, ix, iy, kind, plt, sd, phx, phy, lv) {
    x0 = mod(ix, 2);
    x1 = mod(floor(ix / 2), 2);
    x2 = mod(floor(ix / 4), 2);
    y0 = mod(iy, 2);
    y1 = mod(floor(iy / 2), 2);
    y2 = mod(floor(iy / 4), 2);
    mm = 16 * (2 * abs(x0 - y0) + y0) + 4 * (2 * abs(x1 - y1) + y1) + (2 * abs(x2 - y2) + y2);
    t_bay = (mm + 0.5) / 64;
    ox = switch(plt < 0.5, 0, switch(plt < 1.5, 23, 47));
    oy = switch(plt < 0.5, 0, switch(plt < 1.5, 41, 13));
    gx = ix + ox - floor(phx * 8 + 0.5);
    gy = iy + oy - floor(phy * 8 + 0.5);
    bx = gx + 61 * sd;
    by = gy + 29 * sd;
    bx = bx - 64 * floor(bx / 64);
    by = by - 64 * floor(by / 64);
    t_blue = nearest(in5, vec((bx + 0.5) / 64, (by + 0.5) / 64)).x;
    t_rand = fract(sin(gx * 127.1 + gy * 311.7 + sd * 74.7) * 43758.5453);
    thr = switch(kind < 0.5, t_bay, switch(kind < 1.5, t_blue, t_rand));
    l1 = max(floor(lv + 0.5) - 1, 1);
    q = tone * l1;
    fq = floor(q);
    o = clamp((fq + switch(q - fq > thr, 1, 0)) / l1, 0, 1);
    return switch(tone <= 0, 0, switch(tone >= 1, 1, o));
}

// T029b (Matt, 2026-11-14; FR-022): Bayer's cell follows the plate's own pitch. Returns the read uv and the cell indices.
bay_cell(pp, nx, ny, wd, ht, cellmode) {
    bs = max(floor(pp * ht / 8 + 0.5), 1);
    ix = floor(floor(nx * wd) / bs);
    iy = floor(floor(ny * ht) / bs);
    bx = min(ix * bs + floor(bs / 2), wd - 1);
    by = min(iy * bs + floor(bs / 2), ht - 1);
    return switch(cellmode > 0.5, (bx + 0.5) / wd, nx), switch(cellmode > 0.5, (by + 0.5) / ht, ny), ix, iy;
}

// T028: the Single path (T016b) on one inlet, as a function so Plates can run it per plate. Returns the plate's r, g, b:
// colour (rgb / brightest, at the texel the tone came from) times coverage. nx, ny: the pixel's norm.
single_path(src, px, py, nx, ny, is_line, is_thr, is_bay, dkind, use_jit, cs, sn, pit, phx, phy, asp, wd, ht, soft, aa, shp, jit, sd, lvl, cellmode, lv) {
    qx, qy = lat_xy(px, py, cs, sn, pit, phx, phy);
    ru, rv = read_uv(qx, qy, is_line, cs, sn, pit, phx, phy, asp, wd, ht);
    cov = cover(qx, qy, is_line, rd(ru, rv, 3, src), soft, aa, shp);
    cu = ru;
    cv = rv;
    if (use_jit > 0.5) {
        cov = dot_jit(qx, qy, 3, src, cs, sn, pit, phx, phy, asp, wd, ht, soft, aa, shp, jit, sd);
        cu, cv = jit_uv(qx, qy, cs, sn, pit, phx, phy, asp, wd, ht, jit, sd);
    }
    bu, bv, ix, iy = bay_cell(pit, nx, ny, wd, ht, cellmode);
    plt = switch(src < 0.5, 2, src - 1);
    cov = switch(is_thr > 0.5, thresh(rd(nx, ny, 3, src), lvl, soft),
                 switch(is_bay > 0.5, dither(rd(bu, bv, 3, src), ix, iy, dkind, plt, sd, phx, phy, lv), cov));
    cu = switch(is_thr > 0.5, nx, switch(is_bay > 0.5, bu, cu));
    cv = switch(is_thr > 0.5, ny, switch(is_bay > 0.5, bv, cv));
    cr = rd(cu, cv, 0, src);
    cg = rd(cu, cv, 1, src);
    cb = rd(cu, cv, 2, src);
    ct = max(max(cr, cg), cb);
    nrm = switch(ct > 0, 1 / max(ct, 0.000000000001), 0) * cov;
    return cr * nrm, cg * nrm, cb * nrm;
}

Param screen(0);
Param pitch(0.012);
Param scale_r(1);
Param scale_g(1);
Param scale_b(1);
Param angle_r(15);
Param angle_g(75);
Param angle_b(45);
Param phase_r_x(0);
Param phase_r_y(0);
Param phase_g_x(0);
Param phase_g_y(0);
Param phase_b_x(0);
Param phase_b_y(0);
Param softness(0.1);
Param dot_shape(0);
Param jitter(0);
Param seed(1);
Param level(0.5);
Param plate_mode(0);
Param bayer_cell(1);
Param levels(2);
Param bypass_gate(0);
Param plate1_on(0);
Param plate2_on(0);
Param plate3_on(0);
Param width(1920);
Param height(1080);

zr = zap(sample(in1, norm).x);
zg = zap(sample(in1, norm).y);
zb = zap(sample(in1, norm).z);
za = zap(sample(in1, norm).w);

wd = max(width, 1);
ht = max(height, 1);
asp = wd / ht;
px = (norm.x - 0.5) * asp;
py = norm.y - 0.5;
// T029b (FR-022): each plate's pitch is pitch * its scale; the lattice, phase, edge ramp, jitter and Bayer cell follow it
pit_r = max(pitch * scale_r, 0.0001);
pit_g = max(pitch * scale_g, 0.0001);
pit_b = max(pitch * scale_b, 0.0001);
aa_r = 1 / (pit_r * ht);
aa_g = 1 / (pit_g * ht);
aa_b = 1 / (pit_b * ht);
soft = clamp(softness, 0, 1);
shp = clamp(dot_shape, 0, 1);
is_line = switch(abs(screen - 1) < 0.5, 1, 0);
is_thr = switch(abs(screen - 2) < 0.5, 1, 0);
is_bay = switch(screen > 2.5, 1, 0);          // Bayer, Blue, Random: the dither screens (T035)
dkind = clamp(floor(screen + 0.5) - 3, 0, 2);
jit = clamp(jitter, 0, 1);
use_jit = switch(jit > 0, 1, 0) * switch(screen < 0.5, 1, 0);
d2r = pi / 180;

// red plate
csr = snap0(cos(angle_r * d2r));
snr = snap0(sin(angle_r * d2r));
qxr, qyr = lat_xy(px, py, csr, snr, pit_r, phase_r_x, phase_r_y);
ur, vr = read_uv(qxr, qyr, is_line, csr, snr, pit_r, phase_r_x, phase_r_y, asp, wd, ht);
tone_r = zap(nearest(in1, vec(ur, vr)).x);
cov_r = cover(qxr, qyr, is_line, tone_r, soft, aa_r, shp);
if (use_jit > 0.5) {
    cov_r = dot_jit(qxr, qyr, 0, 0, csr, snr, pit_r, phase_r_x, phase_r_y, asp, wd, ht, soft, aa_r, shp, jit, seed);
}

// green plate
csg = snap0(cos(angle_g * d2r));
sng = snap0(sin(angle_g * d2r));
qxg, qyg = lat_xy(px, py, csg, sng, pit_g, phase_g_x, phase_g_y);
ug, vg = read_uv(qxg, qyg, is_line, csg, sng, pit_g, phase_g_x, phase_g_y, asp, wd, ht);
tone_g = zap(nearest(in1, vec(ug, vg)).y);
cov_g = cover(qxg, qyg, is_line, tone_g, soft, aa_g, shp);
if (use_jit > 0.5) {
    cov_g = dot_jit(qxg, qyg, 1, 0, csg, sng, pit_g, phase_g_x, phase_g_y, asp, wd, ht, soft, aa_g, shp, jit, seed);
}

// blue plate
csb = snap0(cos(angle_b * d2r));
snb = snap0(sin(angle_b * d2r));
qxb, qyb = lat_xy(px, py, csb, snb, pit_b, phase_b_x, phase_b_y);
ub, vb = read_uv(qxb, qyb, is_line, csb, snb, pit_b, phase_b_x, phase_b_y, asp, wd, ht);
tone_b = zap(nearest(in1, vec(ub, vb)).z);
cov_b = cover(qxb, qyb, is_line, tone_b, soft, aa_b, shp);
if (use_jit > 0.5) {
    cov_b = dot_jit(qxb, qyb, 2, 0, csb, snb, pit_b, phase_b_x, phase_b_y, asp, wd, ht, soft, aa_b, shp, jit, seed);
}

// T025: Threshold and the dithers (Bayer; Blue and Random, T035) replace the lattice, per pixel
bur, bvr, ixr, iyr = bay_cell(pit_r, norm.x, norm.y, wd, ht, bayer_cell);
bgu, bvg, ixg, iyg = bay_cell(pit_g, norm.x, norm.y, wd, ht, bayer_cell);
bu, bv, ixb, iyb = bay_cell(pit_b, norm.x, norm.y, wd, ht, bayer_cell);
cov_r = switch(is_thr > 0.5, thresh(zr, level, soft), switch(is_bay > 0.5, dither(rd(bur, bvr, 0, 0), ixr, iyr, dkind, 0, seed, phase_r_x, phase_r_y, levels), cov_r));
cov_g = switch(is_thr > 0.5, thresh(zg, level, soft), switch(is_bay > 0.5, dither(rd(bgu, bvg, 1, 0), ixg, iyg, dkind, 1, seed, phase_g_x, phase_g_y, levels), cov_g));
cov_b = switch(is_thr > 0.5, thresh(zb, level, soft), switch(is_bay > 0.5, dither(rd(bu, bv, 2, 0), ixb, iyb, dkind, 2, seed, phase_b_x, phase_b_y, levels), cov_b));

// T016b: Single, one plate at the blue plate's angle and phase (single_path on in1)
is_single = switch(plate_mode > 0.5, 1, 0);
sr, sg, sb = single_path(0, px, py, norm.x, norm.y, is_line, is_thr, is_bay, dkind, use_jit, csb, snb, pit_b, phase_b_x, phase_b_y,
                         asp, wd, ht, soft, aa_b, shp, jit, seed, level, bayer_cell, levels);
oa = za;
// T028: Plates, inlets 1 to 3 as Single at the R, G, B sets; summed, clamped; alpha the largest connected plate's
if (plate_mode > 1.5) {
    r1, g1, b1 = single_path(1, px, py, norm.x, norm.y, is_line, is_thr, is_bay, dkind, use_jit, csr, snr, pit_r, phase_r_x, phase_r_y,
                             asp, wd, ht, soft, aa_r, shp, jit, seed, level, bayer_cell, levels);
    r2, g2, b2 = single_path(2, px, py, norm.x, norm.y, is_line, is_thr, is_bay, dkind, use_jit, csg, sng, pit_g, phase_g_x, phase_g_y,
                             asp, wd, ht, soft, aa_g, shp, jit, seed, level, bayer_cell, levels);
    r3, g3, b3 = single_path(3, px, py, norm.x, norm.y, is_line, is_thr, is_bay, dkind, use_jit, csb, snb, pit_b, phase_b_x, phase_b_y,
                             asp, wd, ht, soft, aa_b, shp, jit, seed, level, bayer_cell, levels);
    k1 = step(0.5, plate1_on);
    k2 = step(0.5, plate2_on);
    k3 = step(0.5, plate3_on);
    sr = clamp(k1 * r1 + k2 * r2 + k3 * r3, 0, 1);
    sg = clamp(k1 * g1 + k2 * g2 + k3 * g3, 0, 1);
    sb = clamp(k1 * b1 + k2 * b2 + k3 * b3, 0, 1);
    oa = max(max(k1 * zap(nearest(in2, norm).w), k2 * zap(nearest(in3, norm).w)), k3 * zap(nearest(in4, norm).w));
}
o_r = mix(cov_r, sr, is_single);
o_g = mix(cov_g, sg, is_single);
o_b = mix(cov_b, sb, is_single);

out1 = mix(vec(o_r, o_g, o_b, oa), vec(zr, zg, zb, za), step(0.5, bypass_gate));
